# Symbulator circuit book

title: Circuits for Lesson 10 of the Tutorial

[AS7's Example 13.1 (mutual inductance in jOhm)]

e,1,0,12
r1,1,2,-4j
r2,2,0,5j
m,r2,r3,3j
r3,3,0,6j
r4,3,0,12

analysis: ac
omega: omega
note: The coils are given in jOhm, so they are r elements with imaginary values and the mutual matches. The dotted end of each coupled element is named first.
rounding: 4
si: no
units: yes
rms: no
polar: yes


