[AS7's Figure 13.33 (ideal transformer, symbolic)]

t,2,3,1,n
r2,3,4,z2
e2,4,0,vs2

analysis: dc
tool: th
n1: 2
n2: 0
note: The transformer refers the source by the turns ratio and the impedance by its square, which is what an ideal one does. Everything here is a name.
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


[AS7's Example 13.8 (ideal transformer, opposite dots)]

e,1,0,120
r1,1,2,4-6j
t,2,3,1,-2
ro,3,0,20

analysis: ac
omega: omega
note: One turn count is negative because the dots are of opposite polarity; which of the two you negate makes no difference.
rounding: 4
si: no
units: yes
rms: yes
polar: yes
evaluate: -se
